<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manikongo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manikongo was the title of the king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a>. The manikongo ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">Mbanza Kongo</a> over provinces such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soyo">Soyo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbata">Mbata</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nsundi">Nsundi</a>, governing through appointed officials and tribute. The office was central to the military and political organisation of the Kongo Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manikongo.jpg" alt="Manikongo" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kongo_audience.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
